  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where you switch",
      "items": [
        "The Garrick App shows where every thread stands and opens any of them at its next action, on the Mac or in a browser",
        "Say “hold this” when you are interrupted and “back” when you return. cmux gives each thread a terminal tab; Obsidian and phone access are optional too"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The record",
      "items": [
        "Each thread has one resume point: what is done, the next action, and what was only in your head",
        "Meetings keeps every conversation, Knowledge what you read. All of it is plain Markdown in git, on your Mac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The guard, and the agent under it",
      "items": [
        "Claude Code or Codex does the work, in its desktop app or a terminal, and reads the rules first",
        "Walls you declare tell it whose material never meets. A check before every commit catches links, names and copied wording across a wall, within limits: see Principles and limits"
      ]
    }
  ]
